1..20
ok 1 - Block with explicit $_ has one formal parameter
ok 2 - Block with implicit $_ has one formal parameter
ok 3 - $_ in bare block defaults to outer
ok 4 - but it is only a default
ok 5 - no implicit $_ usage checking
ok 6 - $_ gets assigned but is not used
ok 7 - {$_} is arity 0, of course
ok 8 - Blocks that uses $_ implicitly have arity 0
ok 9 - {$_} is count 1
ok 10 - Blocks that uses $_ implicitly have count 1
ok 11 - -> {} is arity 0
ok 12 - Even when we use $_>
ok 13 - $_ is lexical here
ok 14 - Even with parameters
ok 15 - But not when the parameter is $_
# Subtest: Placeholders not allowed in ->
    1..2
    ok 1 - 'sub () { -> { $^a }.() }' died
    ok 2 - right exception type (X::Signature::Placeholder)
ok 16 - Placeholders not allowed in ->
ok 17 - ->{} is arity 0, again
# Subtest: Placeholders not allowed in sub()
    1..2
    ok 1 - 'sub () { $^foo }.(42)' died
    ok 2 - right exception type (X::Signature::Placeholder)
ok 18 - Placeholders not allowed in sub()
ok 19 - outer $_ is seen within nested blocks
ok 20 - hash like block with implicit parameter
